# Generated CV fixtures for the test suite. Rebuild with:
#   python tests/make_fixtures.py
tests/fixtures/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# assets/vendor/ is deliberately NOT ignored. GitHub Pages serves what is in the
# repository, so the document libraries have to be committed for the deployed app
# to read a CV without contacting a third-party CDN. Fetch them with:
#   python tools/fetch_libraries.py

# Enrichment pipeline HTTP cache: rebuildable, not source.
tools/market_data/.cache/

# The OCR engine IS committed, unlike PDF.js and Mammoth.
#
# Those two fall back to a CDN cleanly when absent. Tesseract cannot: a Web
# Worker may not be created from a cross-origin script, so a CDN fallback hangs
# on the first page instead of failing. GitHub Pages deploys the branch as-is
# with no build step to fetch it, so the choice is between 26 MB in the
# repository and a feature that does not work in production.
